## Approach — compose the shipped sub-component surfaces (no reimplementation)

The eight web `security-access/*` leaves are ALREADY shipped as native P4 feature-view
parity units under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/` (each `*.swift` View + `*.Model.swift`
`@Observable` model + `*.Adapter.swift` seam + `*.Previews/*.Tests/*.strings`):
`SummaryStatsRow`, `SecurityStatusCards`, `WindowStatusDetail`, `LiveVehicleState`,
`SentryModeChart`, `SecurityStatistics`, `EventHistoryTable`, `EventTimeline`.

Per the `SystemPage` precedent (a page composes already-shipped panels, never duplicating
their logic), `SecurityAccessPage` COMPOSES these surfaces. The page owns only the web
page-level chrome + the two page-owned `GlassPanel`s, and binds the eight sub-models through
`SecurityAccessPageModel`, each seeded from one cohesive sample dataset via the surfaces' OWN
public in-memory sources (mirroring each surface's loaded preview). No sub-component types or
logic are re-declared (an initial reimplementation collided with the shipped
`SentryDayBucket` / `SecuritySignal` / `SecurityMetricTile` and was removed).

Files (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/):
  - SecurityAccessPage.swift            — View: chrome + GlassPanel1 + GlassPanel2 + composition
  - SecurityAccessPageModel.swift       — @Observable model (vehicles query + twin facts + 8 sub-models)
  - SecurityAccessPageModel.Sample.swift— sample vehicle listing + the 8 sub-model factories
  - SecurityAccessRouteRegistration.swift— `.securityAccess` route registration
Navigation: `AppRoute.securityAccess` (+ pathSegment `security-access`, systemImage, `.vehicle`
  group) in Sources/App/AppRoute.swift; wired into Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift route registry.
Strings: 108 `admin.security.*` + `route.securityAccess` + `range.*` keys added to
  `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (79 reuse the existing `translation.admin.security.*`
  localizations; 29 en + web defaults).
Ledger: apps/parity/apple-ledger.json — `page:admin/SecurityAccess` rows added for
  apple-macos + apple-ios (covered 9 / required 9).

